X-WR-CALNAME:Sun Path — Four Turnings 2026
X-WR-CALDESC:The four hinges of the year — solstices and equinoxes — at their exact UTC instants. From pilgrimapp.org/sunpath.

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:turning-spring-equinox-2026@pilgrimapp.org
DTSTAMP:20260101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260320T144600Z
DTEND:20260320T154600Z
SUMMARY:Spring Equinox 2026 · 春分
DESCRIPTION:The sun crosses the equator. Day equals night across the Earth.\n\nFrom here, northern days grow until summer solstice.\n\nhttps://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-spring-equinox
URL:https://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-spring-equinox
CATEGORIES:Equinox,Astronomy
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Spring Equinox tomorrow — day will equal night
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:turning-summer-solstice-2026@pilgrimapp.org
DTSTAMP:20260101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260621T082600Z
DTEND:20260621T092600Z
SUMMARY:Summer Solstice 2026 · 夏至
DESCRIPTION:The sun stands at its furthest north. The longest northern day.\n\nFrom here, northern days shorten until winter solstice.\n\nhttps://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-summer-solstice
URL:https://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-summer-solstice
CATEGORIES:Solstice,Astronomy
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Summer Solstice tomorrow — the longest light
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:turning-autumn-equinox-2026@pilgrimapp.org
DTSTAMP:20260101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260923T000600Z
DTEND:20260923T010600Z
SUMMARY:Autumn Equinox 2026 · 秋分
DESCRIPTION:The sun crosses the equator again. Day equals night.\n\nFrom here, northern nights grow longer until winter solstice.\n\nhttps://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-autumn-equinox
URL:https://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-autumn-equinox
CATEGORIES:Equinox,Astronomy
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Autumn Equinox tomorrow — northern days begin to shorten
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:turning-winter-solstice-2026@pilgrimapp.org
DTSTAMP:20260101T000000Z
DTSTART:20261221T205100Z
DTEND:20261221T215100Z
SUMMARY:Winter Solstice 2026 · 冬至
DESCRIPTION:The sun reaches its furthest south. The longest northern night.\n\nFrom here, light returns. Northern days grow until summer solstice.\n\nhttps://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-winter-solstice
URL:https://pilgrimapp.org/sunpath/2026-winter-solstice
CATEGORIES:Solstice,Astronomy
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Winter Solstice tomorrow — the longest dark, and the turning back toward light
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

